  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (categorizing outcomes as probable based on probability > 1/n and computing the average of such outcomes) is not present in the verbal report. The individual does not refer to the threshold (1/3 or 1/2), does not identify which outcomes are probable, nor does the individual compute or compare the average of probable outcomes. Instead, the justification is based on the intuitive comparison of the chance of losing nothing (75% vs. 50%) and a general reluctance to play. This reflects a different reasoning process—risk aversion or preference for certainty—rather than the formal application of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason. The reasoning process described does not align with the rule of the decision reason in either content or structure.",
